{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1339281-finally-getting-into-werewolf-20th","id":1339281,"title":"FINALLY getting into Werewolf 20th!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-03T18:28:06-07:00","id":1339281,"title":"FINALLY getting into Werewolf 20th!","content":"Friend surprised me and picked me up the Deluxe Edition of the 20th. After all these years I'm moving past 2e. My question is this, what 20th stuff should I focus on getting first? I have quite a bit of 1e/2e stuff that I can still use. For example:<br /> <br /> Book of the Wyrm (2nd), Weaver, Wyld.<br /> All the 1e Tribe Books<br /> Most of the Breed Books.<br /> First Book of the Umbra, ST, and Player's Guide.<br /> Random things like the Book of Auspices.<br /> All of the Wild West material (Even the playing cards - lol)<br /> <br /> With a lot of the older books on hand, what would you peeps suggest getting next?<br /> <br /> On a side note, I picked up a Book of The Wyrm ST screen for cheap (Physical). I'm guessing all the information contains in the WW20th, Changing Breeds, and Book of the Wyrm ST screens are the same? Hope so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25442,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25442-tikank","user":"TIKank","date":". 10-03-2019, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25442-tikank","name":"TIKank","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T10:53:44-07:00","id":1339408,"title":"","content":"The two books I think give you the most bang for your buck in WtA20 are Book of the Wyrm and Changing Breeds. <br /> <br /> Book of the Wyrm because I think each edition has something new and interesting that can be used with inspiration and ideas you pulled from previous editions. I think you can get some great synergies with Wyrm20 and Wyrm 2nd. <br /> <br /> Changing Breeds gives you updated gifts for the breeds. Some updated or modified lore. Information on the Hegeyokai and Ahadi. It also has 3 extinct breeds you can use as a &quot;they're back&quot; story or historical game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/918-geeklord1","name":"geeklord1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar918_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T21:31:19-07:00","id":1339760,"title":"","content":"A book that I really, really, *really* suggest on top of those two is <i>Changing Ways</i>;<br /> <br /> t is, in my opinion, the best fluff book for Werewolf you can get your hands on by far.<br /> One of the big things it explains is how it *feels* to be a shifter. To come to age, to feel the changes. From the turmoil inside, to how it feels to shift, how much healing actually *hurts*, to the mental changes and going-ons. It explains the mental and physical state of being a shifter in really, really good detail.<br /> It has a whole special chapter regarding Metis, and how they grow up and handle their lives, as well as going into depth in general about the Pack life. Also details about how the frick shifter pregnancies work, and the problems (and non-problems) that come with it.<br /> <br /> Really, get that book. If you want players to get a good dose of &quot;Garou: The Daily Life&quot;, this is the book to let them read.<br /> Plus, on the non-fluff side contains a few additional mechanics for Primal-Urge rolls, new Metis deformities, rites and totems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T13:24:10-07:00","id":1340287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1339281-finally-getting-into-werewolf-20th?p=1339760#post1339760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A book that I really, really, *really* suggest on top of those two is <i>Changing Ways</i>;<br /> <br /> t is, in my opinion, the best fluff book for Werewolf you can get your hands on by far.<br /> One of the big things it explains is how it *feels* to be a shifter. To come to age, to feel the changes. From the turmoil inside, to how it feels to shift, how much healing actually *hurts*, to the mental changes and going-ons. It explains the mental and physical state of being a shifter in really, really good detail.<br /> It has a whole special chapter regarding Metis, and how they grow up and handle their lives, as well as going into depth in general about the Pack life. Also details about how the frick shifter pregnancies work, and the problems (and non-problems) that come with it.<br /> <br /> Really, get that book. If you want players to get a good dose of &quot;Garou: The Daily Life&quot;, this is the book to let them read.<br /> Plus, on the non-fluff side contains a few additional mechanics for Primal-Urge rolls, new Metis deformities, rites and totems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changing Ways is fatally flawed in a number of ways, like how it tries to make Garou out to be like novas from Aberrant or the Uratha from W:tF in the capacity to stay super-thin or have mundane medical procedures or drugs fail on them even in breed form (for non-metis), making them unable to stay in contact with human society or pass for a normal human. It's a complete wreck of an attempt to blend Forsaken material into Apocalypse; a how-to of how not to do it, even before touching on how one of the &quot;this never works, usually&quot; medical procedures in question is abortion, or how the Garou Nation, including even the Black Furies, somehow takes a &quot;Gaia doesn't make mistakes!&quot; route on the issue of trans Garou. Lovely and cogent theology, I'm sure that there's no dispute in the Nation about how much attention Gaia pays to the Garou, specifically, being at or above Celstine status (usually a good ways above) and hence very distant and all.<br /> <br /> Now, the Furies have been presented as something of gender essentialists in Revised, but given who wrote that book and what he's done, I'd kick that shit to the curb from a rocket car and let it roll to a stop off in the distance in a long trail of blood, torn flesh, and disarticulated bones. It can join perpetually horny land-walking Rokea (technically pre-dating McFarland's participation, but not less noisome) in the pile of things that need to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T14:35:01-07:00","id":1340301,"title":"","content":"I can't really agree with most of this, really.<br /> I mean, when we start on the topic of shifters having big troubles with functioning in normal society, let's start with about half the population trying to <i>actively avoid you at all costs</i> at Rage <b>4</b>. There are two of five auspices that already have or beat that at character generation. Even Rage 3 brings this to a &quot;mere&quot; 40% of folks out there trying not to interact with you in any way. So the <i>majority</i> of the available auspices actually have more than just a little bit of trouble even just having a nice time out in town from the get-go - or even finding a job.. This isn't Changing Ways, this is the core book dating back to 2nd ed. And it's one of the big, BIG reasons why Kin are so important to the functioning of the Nation. Including cash flow. Nobody will hire you if the customer base just halves.<br /> <br /> Second, the book aaaaaactually states that medical procedures and drugs are working <i>absolutely fine</i> in breed form - aside of (weirdly, I agree, and not quite logical. IMO ignorable) chemical forms of Abortion - because of the lack of accelerated healing. I suggest re-reading that part. The opinion of the Garou nation on these kind of things miiight be a different matter though, as par for the course.<br /> <br /> The trans stuff I shouldn't touch with a ten-foot pole, but given that the Nation even has issues with same sex romance because they feel it gets in the way of performing certain duties....yeeeah. It's on the other hand not suprising.<br /> <br /> Dunno about the Revised parts you mention - I'm unfamiliar with that part, or the authors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-08-2019, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T01:34:46-07:00","id":1340384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1339281-finally-getting-into-werewolf-20th?p=1340287#post1340287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Changing Ways is fatally flawed in a number of ways, like how it tries to make Garou out to be like novas from Aberrant or the Uratha from W:tF in the capacity to stay super-thin or have mundane medical procedures or drugs fail on them even in breed form (for non-metis), making them unable to stay in contact with human society or pass for a normal human. It's a complete wreck of an attempt to blend Forsaken material into Apocalypse; a how-to of how not to do it, even before touching on how one of the &quot;this never works, usually&quot; medical procedures in question is abortion, or how the Garou Nation, including even the Black Furies, somehow takes a &quot;Gaia doesn't make mistakes!&quot; route on the issue of trans Garou. Lovely and cogent theology, I'm sure that there's no dispute in the Nation about how much attention Gaia pays to the Garou, specifically, being at or above Celstine status (usually a good ways above) and hence very distant and all.<br /> <br /> Now, the Furies have been presented as something of gender essentialists in Revised, but given who wrote that book and what he's done, I'd kick that shit to the curb from a rocket car and let it roll to a stop off in the distance in a long trail of blood, torn flesh, and disarticulated bones. It can join perpetually horny land-walking Rokea (technically pre-dating McFarland's participation, but not less noisome) in the pile of things that need to go.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed, there some good stuff hidden in it but so much garbage its not really worth the dig.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T06:15:25-07:00","id":1340401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1339281-finally-getting-into-werewolf-20th?p=1340384#post1340384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed, there some good stuff hidden in it but so much garbage its not really worth the dig.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really a mixed bag, but mostly sparks and bulls*t. It's like SOME of the writers had a very divergent WW experince and tried to enforce it &amp; their house rules on the public.<br /> <br /> Hey, but some of the parts are JUST narrated by a few werewolf, whose creditibility is questionable. Maybe they were infected by the Wyrm and try to corrupt the soul of the Nation from inside.<br /> <br /> Back to the first question (Here I edited it, 'cause originaly, I was a fool.):<br /> 1) W20 - Book of the Wyrm<br /> 2) Shattered Dreams<br /> 3) Changing Breeds<br /> 4) Kinfolk","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":562,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","user":"Lachdanan","date":". 10-17-2019, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T00:53:51-07:00","id":1341230,"title":"","content":"There were some informative passages in the Storyteller's Handbook revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T05:50:42-07:00","id":1341619,"title":"","content":"Book of the Wyrm 20th is a must have. The new rendition of Umbra is also rather good. Everything else is up to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T15:38:37-07:00","id":1341722,"title":"","content":"Changing Ways is not a good book, because it takes the 20th edition being more aware of social issues and forgets them. There is an illogical rape-rumour about two tribes, wendigo never had metis before white people, they took the term from Forsaken about packs etc.<br /> <br /> But every other 20th edition book? Absolutely great. Umbra has a much more robust look into the spirit world, Wyrm has AMAZING amount of info plus BSDs that are very different from revised. Changing Breeds has so much info, Shattered Dreams both has some hard hitting looks into Australian colonization and just fun time travel.<br /> <br /> Instead of Changing Ways, I'd recommend Players Guide to Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T03:58:25-07:00","id":1341832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1339281-finally-getting-into-werewolf-20th?p=1341722#post1341722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BSDs that are very different from revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what ways?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T09:29:19-07:00","id":1341876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1339281-finally-getting-into-werewolf-20th?p=1341832#post1341832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In what ways?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, the revised BSDs are all about freeing the Wyrm and spreading corruption. They also hold very close ties to the White Howlers and picts.<br /> <br /> In 20th, BSDs are no longer such an unified force and some have chosen to live like the war is won, essentially becoming BSD versions of the Bone Gnawer rabble. There is also zero ties to Howlers as the BSDs have moved past them AGES ago. They now focus on personal projects and have looser ties even in packs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T18:05:15-08:00","id":1349224,"title":"","content":"So, is it worth it to pick up a copy of Werewolf the Apocalypse 20, or should I stay content with my old first edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T02:22:54-08:00","id":1349303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwolf8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1339281-finally-getting-into-werewolf-20th?p=1349224#post1349224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, is it worth it to pick up a copy of Werewolf the Apocalypse 20, or should I stay content with my old first edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends what your expectations are for W20.<br /> <br /> Personally, I own multiple copies, because I like WtA that much. But I was disappointed in the book in general and some directions WtA was going. All in all, it is probably less expensive to buy Werewolf revised, if you want to get way from your 1st Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}